Jesus was in the house of Bethany. He was in the house of a man named Simon, who had a skin disease.
A woman came to Jesus with a special, very expensive perfume bottle. She poured the perfume on his head while he was at the table.
When the students saw this, they were angry. "Why is there so much waste?" they asked.
The perfume could have been sold for a high price. The money could have been given to the poor.
Jesus knew this. He said to them, "Why do you trouble this woman? She has done a beautiful thing to me."
There will always be poor people with you. But you will not always find me.
