One of the twelve went to the chief priests. His name was Judas Iscariot.
He asked, "What will you give me if I hand Jesus over to you?" So they counted out thirty pieces of silver for him.
Since then, Judas had been watching for an opportune time to hand Jesus over to them. The Last Supper.
It was the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread. The disciples came to Jesus and said, "Where do you want us to prepare for you to eat the Passover meal?"
Go to a certain man in the city. Tell him, 'The teacher says: "My hour has come near. I will go to celebrate the Passover at your house with my disciples."'"
So the disciples did what Jesus had instructed them. They prepared the Passover meal.
When evening came, Jesus was at the table with the twelve.
While he was eating, he said, "What I am about to tell you is true. One of you will betray me into the hands of my enemies."
The disciples were very much grieved, and each of them began to say to him, "Is it I, Lord?"
Jesus answered, "The one who has dipped his hand with me in the bowl will betray me.
The son of man will go away just as it is written about him. But woe to the one who betrays the son of man! It would have been better for him if he had not been born.
It was Judas who was going to betray him. He said, "I am not, Teacher, am I?" Jesus answered, "You have said so."
While they were eating, Jesus took bread, thanked, broke it and gave it to the disciples, and said: "Take, eat, this is my body."
Then he took the cup. He thanked and gave it to them. He said, "Drink all of it from it."
This is my blood of the New Covenant. It was poured out for the forgiveness of the sins of many.
Here's what I tell you. From now on, I will never again drink wine with you until the day I drink it with you in my Father's kingdom.
