Peter replied, "All the others may well go back on account of you. But I never will."
"What I am about to tell you is true," Jesus answered. "This very night before the rooster crows, you yourself will disown me three times."
But Peter said, "I will never die with you. " And he said, "I do not know what you are talking about. " And immediately, while he was still speaking, a cock crowed. And Peter remembered the word that Jesus had spoken to him: "Before the cock crows, you will deny me three times. " And he went out and wept bitterly. And the other disciples went to a place to pray. And Jesus went to a place called Gethsemane and told his disciples, "Stay here and pray so that you will not fall into temptation. " And Jesus went a little further and fell to the ground. And he prayed, "My Father, if it is possible, may this cup be taken away from me. Yet not my will, but yours be done. " And an angel from heaven appeared to him and gave him strength. And being in anguish, he prayed more earnestly, and his sweat was like drops of blood falling to the ground. And when he got up from prayer, he went to the disciples and found them asleep. And he said to Peter, "Are you still sleeping? Get up and pray so that you will not fall into temptation. " And while he was speaking, there came a crowd, and the man named Judas, one of the twelve, went ahead of them and drew near to Jesus to kiss him. But Jesus said to him, "Judas, would you betray the Son of Man with a kiss? " And those who were with Jesus saw what would happen and asked, "Lord, should we use swords? " And one of them struck the servant of the high priest and cut off his ear. But Jesus said, "No more of this! " And he touched the man's ear and healed him. Then Jesus said to the crowd, "Have you come out with swords and clubs to capture me? I was with you every day in the temple, and you did not lay hands on me. " And the crowd said, "This is his disciple! " But one of the disciples of Jesus, who was with him when he was arrested, went with a crowd and laid hold of one of the men who were with Jesus. And he said, "This man was with Jesus of Nazareth! " But Jesus said, "My kingdom is not of this world. If my kingdom were of this world, my servants would be fighting to prevent my arrest by the Jews. "But now my kingdom is not from here. "Jesus said to Pilate, "My kingdom would not be subject to observation; my kingdom is not of this world. If my kingdom were of this world, my servants would be fighting to prevent my arrest by the Jews. But as it is, my kingdom is not from here. "The Jews answered him, 'We are not stoning you for any good work, but for blasphemy, because you, a man, claim to be God. ' Jesus answered them, 'Is it not written in your law, "I have said you are gods"? If he called them gods, to whom the word of God came (and the Scripture cannot be broken), what about the One whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world? Do you not believe that I am the One? If not, believe me because of my works. ' "I tell you the truth, everyone who sins is a slave to sin. The slave is not able to stay in the house forever; the master will either come back and take him to be punished, or he will cut him free and make him a full brother. " "My kingdom is not of this world. If my kingdom were of this world, my servants would be fighting to prevent my arrest by the Jews. But as it is, my kingdom is not from here."
Then Jesus, with his disciples, went out to an isolated place called Gethsemane. And he said to them, "Sit here, while I go yonder to pray."
Peter took with him James and John, the sons of Zebedee, and he began to feel sorrow and distress.
Then he said to them, "My heart is deeply troubled. I feel the coming of death. Stay here and keep watch with me."
He went a little further. Then he fell face forward on the ground. He prayed, saying, "Abba, if you are willing, take this cup from me. Yet not my will, but yours be done."
