And those who had seized Jesus brought him to Caiaphas the high priest. And with him were assembled the chief priests and the elders of the people.
Not too far away, Peter followed Jesus. He went straight to the courtyard of the chief priest. He entered and sat down with the guards to see what would happen.
The chief priests and all the council were seeking what they might use against Jesus. They desired to put him to death.
But they found no evidence, although many false witnesses were brought in. Finally, two other witnesses came forward.
They said, "This man claimed, 'I can destroy God's house. And I can rebuild it from scratch in three days.'"
Then the chief priests and the scribes stood up. And they asked Jesus, "Do you not hear their testimony? How can you say these things about these men?"
But Jesus remained silent. The high priest said to him, "I adjure you by the living God, tell us if you are the Christ, the Son of God."
"Yes, it is as you say," Jesus answered. "But this is what I tell all of you. In the coming days, you will see the Son of Man seated at the right hand of the Mighty One. And you will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds of heaven."
Then the High Priest rent his clothes. And he said, "He hath spoken a very great and a wicked blasphemy against God! Why do we need any more witnesses than this? You have heard him say this wicked thing."
"What do you think?" they answered: "He must die!"
Then they licked his face. One of them punched him with his fist. Others slapped him.
They said, "Jesus, speak to us, who struck you?" Peter says, "I don't know Jesus."
